1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Open the practice files folder in the library window.

2
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Find the C.Details.C.EditRibbon file.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Drag it to the 2D or 3D window in the T-shirt wrap folder.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
In the 3D T-shirt wrap folder, select the display arrangement point.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Place the ribbon on the arrangement point.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:54,000
In the purple wrap folder arranged by the attribute editor, adjust the version location.

7
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Use the free sewing line tool to mix the ribbon with the sleeve.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Use the free sewing line tool to mix the ribbon with the sleeve.

9
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Use the free sewing line tool to mix the ribbon with the sleeve.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Use the full ribbon tool to make the fold lines on the side of the ribbon.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Select the fold arrangement tool in the 3D tool list.

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Click on the newly created fold line.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
A fold arrangement location tool appears.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Use the arrow for half fold the ribbon.

15
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
This is how to make the fold arrangement tool.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Use the line sewing tool to sew the pattern on both sides of the top and bottom.

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
In the attribute editor, change the sewing line type to TEND.

18
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
After simulation, the pattern will be more even.

19
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Use the editor tool to choose the newly created inner line.

20
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
In the attribute editor, adjust the folding angle to 0 degrees.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Activate simulation.

22
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Apply the settings to 3D clothing.

23
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Use the line sewing tool to sew the pattern on both sides of the top and bottom.

24
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Activate simulation.

25
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Enter the drawing window.

26
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Double-click on the Fabric file.

27
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Press and hold the Ripe 2x2 on the file and move the mouse.

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Loosen the mouse on the pattern on the 2D or 3D window pattern.

29
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Apply the material to the pattern.

30
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Activate simulation.

31
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Apply the settings to the 3D window.

32
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
In the 2D window, use the adjustment panel tool.

33
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Select the heavy pattern.

34
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Press and hold the Ripe 2x2 on the Fabric file.

35
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Align the pattern and copy it.

36
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
In the 3D window, use the positioning tool.

37
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Move the pattern to the model wrist.

38
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Use the line sewing tool to sew the pattern on the sleeve.

39
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Activate simulation.

40
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Use the line sewing tool to add the pattern to the supports.

41
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:11,000
In the 3D window, use the measurement tool to add the pattern to the supports.

42
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
In the 3D window, use the measurement tool to add the pattern to the supports.

43
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Excellent!

44
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Cassie, the checkmark on the top of the skirt is the correct one.

45
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Open the 3D window.

46
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Click the execution button toview.

47
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,000
After the selection is complete, go to thePSAA.

48
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Click the execution button.

49
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Open the 3D window.

